Rusty Client uses programming interfaces that are part of Microsoft Windows (for example the Windows Shell, DPAPI, DWM and the Win32 window functions). These are part of your Windows installation, are not included in Rusty Client, and are licensed to you by Microsoft under the Windows license terms. The C and C++ runtime code that the Microsoft Visual C++ compiler links into Rusty Client is used under the license terms of Microsoft Visual Studio.

